---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import portrait from "../assets/vitor-sacramento.jpg";
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Vitor Sacramento" description="Professional profile, experience and working principles of Vitor Sacramento.">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-head about-head">
      <div class="about-head__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Portfolio / About / Vitor Sacramento</p>
        <h1>Geology, data and software for decisions about territory.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Geologist, data scientist and data engineer working across geospatial intelligence, environmental analysis, data platforms and applied AI.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="#profile">Professional profile ↓</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="about-portrait">
        <Image src={portrait} width={400} height={400} format="webp" quality={84} alt="Portrait of Vitor Sacramento" />
        <figcaption><strong>Vitor Sacramento</strong><span>Geologist · Data scientist · Data engineer</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
    </header>

    <dl class="profile-facts" id="profile">
      <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>Brasília, DF, Brazil<br />Portuguese native · English advanced</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Core practice</dt><dd>Geospatial intelligence, data engineering, applied AI and software systems.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Education</dt><dd>Geology, Universidade de Brasília (UnB)<br />MBA in database management · ADS in progress</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <section class="resume-section section" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="experience-heading">Experience</h2><span class="section-label">Selected timeline</span></div>
      <div class="experience-list">
        <article class="experience-entry"><div class="experience-meta"><span>Sep 2026 — present</span><span>Brasília</span></div><div><h3>Dossel Ambiental</h3><p class="experience-role">Specialist in programming and geotechnologies</p><p>Developing technical solutions that connect environmental questions, geospatial data and automation.</p></div></article>
        <article class="experience-entry"><div class="experience-meta"><span>Apr 2026 — present</span><span>Remote</span></div><div><h3>DigiFarmz.com</h3><p class="experience-role">Data scientist</p><p>Applying data science to agricultural and agroclimatic intelligence, from data preparation through analytical delivery.</p></div></article>
        <article class="experience-entry"><div class="experience-meta"><span>Nov 2025 — present</span><span>Caixa Econômica Federal project</span></div><div><h3>Engesoftware Tecnologia S.A.</h3><p class="experience-role">Senior data administrator</p><p>Working with data administration, structure and quality in a financial technology context.</p></div></article>
        <article class="experience-entry"><div class="experience-meta"><span>2021 — 2025 · resumed 2026</span><span>Brazil</span></div><div><h3>Produzindo Certo</h3><p class="experience-role">Data lead · data scientist · sustainability specialist</p><p>Led data work at the intersection of sustainability, territorial intelligence and decision support.</p></div></article>
        <article class="experience-entry"><div class="experience-meta"><span>2018 — 2020</span><span>Brazil</span></div><div><h3>CENSIPAM</h3><p class="experience-role">Geoprocessing and environmental analysis</p><p>Produced spatial analyses and environmental information for territorial monitoring.</p></div></article>
        <article class="experience-entry"><div class="experience-meta"><span>2013 — 2015</span><span>Brazil</span></div><div><h3>CPRM</h3><p class="experience-role">Geology and geoprocessing</p><p>Built geological and spatial knowledge through analysis, mapping and geoprocessing.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section section" aria-labelledby="teaching-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="teaching-heading">Teaching and education</h2><span class="section-label">Knowledge sharing</span></div>
      <div class="resume-columns">
        <div><h3>Teaching</h3><p>Freelance professor for Ambiental Pro and Anhanguera since 2023, teaching Python, SQL, PostgreSQL/PostGIS, geoprocessing, WebGIS and data science.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Education</h3><ul class="resume-list"><li><strong>Systems analysis and development</strong> — Universidade Católica de Brasília, in progress; expected 2028.</li><li><strong>MBA in database management</strong> — Anhanguera, 2023.</li><li><strong>Bachelor of geology</strong> — Universidade de Brasília, 2015.</li></ul></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-section section" aria-labelledby="skills-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="skills-heading">Tools and areas</h2><span class="section-label">What I bring to a project</span></div>
      <div class="skill-columns">
        <div><h3>Data and software</h3><p>Python, SQL, APIs, PostgreSQL, PostGIS, ETL, data governance, architecture and technical documentation.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Geospatial systems</h3><p>ArcGIS, QGIS, GDAL, remote sensing, spatial analysis, WebGIS and geospatial data products.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Applied intelligence</h3><p>Machine learning, time series, image processing, territorial and agroclimatic intelligence, and decision-support systems.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="prose section">
      <h2>How the disciplines connect</h2><p>Geology provides a way to read the physical world. Geospatial analysis makes spatial relationships explicit. Data engineering gives observations structure, quality and a path into usable systems. Analytical models and software turn that foundation into tools for decisions.</p>
      <h2>Experience and approach</h2><p>My work spans environmental, agroclimatic, technological and financial contexts. I move from diagnosis through implementation: framing questions, structuring data, building APIs and spatial analyses, and making methods understandable. Teaching and documentation are part of this practice because knowledge becomes useful when others can evaluate and apply it.</p>
      <h2>What you can inspect here</h2><p>The <a href="/projects/">selected projects</a> are public experiments in computer vision, media workflows, audio automation, browser privacy and geospatial processing. They show implementation choices and limitations; they are not presented as client deliveries or production services.</p><p>Client and corporate work is described only when ownership and disclosure rights allow it.</p>
      <h2>Professional contact</h2><p><a href="/contact/">GitHub and LinkedIn are the public contact channels</a>. For a longer conversation, share the problem, data, constraints and decision you need to support.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
